## Step 3. {{ titles["3"] }}

Accounts: an AAS journals account (the submission system of the Research Notes of the AAS) and an arXiv account. A first submission to astro-ph.EP may need an endorsement from someone who has already posted there; arXiv tells you when you submit, and the endorsement request goes by email to a colleague who can endorse. The engine cannot submit for you.

The limits (AAS research note guidelines): at most {{ "{:,}".format(f.limits.total) }} words including the title, headings, caption and references, of which up to {{ f.limits.abstract }} are the required abstract, and one figure or one table, not both. The draft is `note/note.tex`, with one figure, `note/figure1`{% if two %} (the folds of both candidates as panels (a) and (b); `note/figure1.svg` and `note/figure1_02.svg` hold each fold alone){% endif %}: {{ f.note_words.total }} words in all ({{ f.note_words.body }} of title, headings, text and caption, {{ f.note_words.abstract }} of abstract, {{ f.note_words.references }} of references; the author block, the keywords and the software line are not counted).
{% if f.note_problems %}
**Over the limit:** {{ f.note_problems | join("; ") }}. Shorten it before you submit.
{% endif %}

1. The author block comes from `docs/author.json` (name, affiliation, email, ORCID): fill in any field it lacks there and build the pack again, then add co-authors.
{% if f.zenodo and f.zenodo.doi and f.zenodo.sandbox %}2. Replace {{ f.zenodo.doi }} (a sandbox DOI) before submission: use the DOI of the record you publish on zenodo.org in step 1.{% elif f.zenodo and f.zenodo.doi %}2. Check that {{ f.zenodo.doi }}, the draft's reserved DOI, matches the published record.{% else %}2. Replace {{ f.doi_shown }} with the Zenodo DOI from step 1.{% endif %}{{ "" }}
3. Read every sentence against `dossier.html`{% if two %} and `dossier_02.html`{% endif %}; the note is built from the stored numbers and says nothing the dossier does not.
4. Compile it with AASTeX v7 (aastex7.cls) and pdflatex; Overleaf has the AAS template. The UAT keywords can be changed in the submission form. {% if f.png %}The figure is `note/figure1.pdf`.{% else %}matplotlib could not be imported when this pack was built, so there is no PDF figure: convert `note/figure1.svg`{% if two %} and `note/figure1_02.svg`{% endif %} to PDF first (Inkscape: `inkscape figure1.svg --export-type=pdf`).{% endif %}

5. Submit it as a Research Note of the AAS. The Note is moderated by an editor for fit, not refereed, and it gets a DOI when published.
6. After acceptance, post the same text to arXiv in astro-ph.EP.

